{
  "an9.13:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 9.13 ",
  "an9.13:0.2": "2. The Lion’s Roar ",
  "an9.13:0.3": "With Koṭṭhita ",
  "an9.13:1.1": "Then Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita went up to Venerable Sāriputta, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an9.13:1.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to Sāriputta: ",
  "an9.13:1.3": "“Reverend Sāriputta, is the spiritual life led under the Buddha for this goal: ‘May deeds to be experienced in this life be experienced by me in lives to come’?” ",
  "an9.13:1.4": "“Certainly not, reverend.” ",
  "an9.13:2.1": "“Then is the spiritual life led under the Buddha for this goal: ‘May deeds to be experienced in lives to come be experienced by me in this life’?” ",
  "an9.13:2.2": "“Certainly not.” ",
  "an9.13:3.1": "“Is the spiritual life led under the Buddha for this goal: ‘May deeds to be experienced as pleasant be experienced by me as painful’?” ",
  "an9.13:3.2": "“Certainly not.” ",
  "an9.13:4.1": "“Then is the spiritual life led under the Buddha for this goal: ‘May deeds to be experienced as painful be experienced by me as pleasant’?” ",
  "an9.13:4.2": "“Certainly not.” ",
  "an9.13:5.1": "“Is the spiritual life led under the Buddha for this goal: ‘May deeds to be experienced when ripe be experienced by me when unripe’?” ",
  "an9.13:5.2": "“Certainly not.” ",
  "an9.13:6.1": "“Then is the spiritual life led under the Buddha for this goal: ‘May deed